Cherit was once a [[Titan]] of [[Lord Casterwill]], the first [[Seeker]], and was called to assist in a confrontation against an [[Nullifiers|ominous figure]]. {{source|Memory Lane}} The two considered each other to be good friends. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}} At some point, however, Cherit's [[Amulet]] was lost, causing him to be constantly anchored to Earth for over 60,000 years. {{source|Huntik Magazine}} Cherit has since revealed that he can no longer recall what his Amulet looks like. {{source|Den vs Harrison}}

During his interactions with humanity, with whom he was quite interested, Cherit noticed that non-Seekers could not communicate with the bond. He, thus, undertook to communicate through speech, though doing so initially proved to be difficult. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

Cherit eventually met and befriended [[Eathon Lambert]] and moved into [[Huntik Foundation]] HQ. {{Source|S2E27}} He would occasionally accompany Eathon on some of his missions against [[the Organization]], once battling [[the Professor]]. {{source|Huntik.com}} {{Source|TCG:OAL-072|OAL-072}} Through Eathon, Cherit made the acquaintance of [[Dante Vale]] and lived with him following the disappearance of Eathon. {{source|S1E01}}
[[File:S2E32 Cherit Lok garden.png|thumb|Cherit and Lok]]
Through Dante, Cherit also met and befriended [[Lok Lambert]], Eathon's son, who had just entered into the world of Seekers and Titans with whom he formed a very strong friendship along their numerous adventures together. {{source|A Seeker Is Born}} Cherit then adventured alongside the team of [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]], [[Dante Vale]], and [[Zhalia Moon]], protecting the world from the evil [[Organization]].
<!--- Adventuring details needed --->

Cherit dreamed of Casterwill summoning a large, darkened figure, calling out his name. {{Source|Memory Lane}}

[[File:S1E24 Cherit.jpg|thumb|Cherit uses his '''Energy Charge''' ability]]
Cherit is capable of flight using his bat-like wings and has displayed the ability to fire energy blast from his mouth, powerful enough to destroy most other Titans with a single blast, although it leaves him exhausted afterward. {{Source|The Casterwill Client}} After training with the Huntik foundation since the fall of [[the Professor]], however, Cherit can fire a blast and still be flying; at one point, he fired twice and was still okay. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}} Still, despite this, he does show some signs of exhaustion after a blast. {{source|Chasing Void}} Cherit has the ability to give other members of his team a power boost through a similar energy blast, which Lok nicknamed 'Energy Charge'. {{source|S1E16}} He also has the ability to perfectly mimic peoples' voices. {{source|Absent Heroes}}

Due to having been invoked for thousands of years, Cherit can speak and decipher many ancient languages, such as when he translated ancient Egyptian so as to aid Lok Lambert and Sophie Casterwill in a puzzle. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} Another case was when he translated ancient French to describe the personality of the Casterwill seer, [[Nostradamus]], whom Cherit described as being friendly. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

Cherit is also an extremely good chess player. He has hinted that he has been around at least since the invention of chess with some indication that he was involved in its invention. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}} He also has some skill at playing the pipe. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}
